# Integer128 power within range

Raises 2 to the 100th power with both operands annotated as int128 to
verify same-type exponentiation stays inside the 128-bit range,
producing 1267650600228229401496703205376.

>>> source
base: int128 = 2
exponent: int128 = 100

power: int128 = base ** exponent
print(power)

<<< stdout
1267650600228229401496703205376

<<< stderr
